### P0-5: Refactor LineElement to Use PathMorphCompositor

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (4 units)
**Dependencies**: P0-3 (PathMorphCompositor), P0-4 (Compositor tests)
**Spec Reference**: gallery/README.md "Element Types" • **Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-09-050344.md Section "RED FLAG #1: Wrong Animation Method"

#### Description
Refactor LineElement to use PathMorphCompositor instead of stroke-dashoffset animation. This aligns implementation with specification requirement for "shoot-in-and-curve" path morphing effect.

**STATUS Evidence**: Current LineElement.addLineDrawing() (lines 144-165) animates stroke-dashoffset, producing wrong visual effect.

#### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Remove stroke-dashoffset logic from LineElement
- [ ] Add PathMorphCompositor integration
- [ ] addPathMorph(startX, startY, duration, delay, easing) method added
- [ ] update(elapsed) calls compositor.update(progress) and sets path 'd' attribute
- [ ] toSVG() delegates to compositor.toSMIL() for path animation
- [ ] Existing line drawing animations use new path morph method
- [ ] Visual comparison confirms match with original HTML

#### Technical Notes
**New Architecture**:
```typescript
class LineElement extends BaseElement {
  private compositor?: PathMorphCompositor;
  private progressTrack?: Track<number>;

  addPathMorph(startX: number, startY: number, duration: number, delay?: number, easing?: string) {
    this.compositor = new PathMorphCompositor({ x: startX, y: startY }, this.pathData.points);
    this.progressTrack = new Track({
      from: 0,
      to: 1,
      duration,
      delay,
      easing
    });
  }

  update(elapsed: number) {
    if (this.compositor && this.progressTrack) {
      const progress = this.progressTrack.getValue(elapsed);
      const pathD = this.compositor.update(progress);
      this.path.setAttribute('d', pathD);
    }
  }
}
```

**Migration Path**:
1. Keep existing addLineDrawing() temporarily for backwards compatibility
2. Add addPathMorph() alongside
3. Update animations to use new method
4. Remove old method after verification

