### P1-3: Implement Animation.exportSVG() with Tests

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (4 units)
**Dependencies**: P0-5 (LineElement using compositor), P1-1 (SVG export validated)
**Spec Reference**: gallery/README.md "SVGExporter.ts" • **Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-09-050344.md Section "SVG Export Capability"

#### Description
Enhance Animation.exportSVG() orchestration to create complete SVG documents with embedded SMIL animations. STATUS shows method exists but is completely untested.

#### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Animation.exportSVG() generates complete SVG document
- [ ] SVG includes xmlns and viewBox attributes
- [ ] All elements contribute their SMIL animations
- [ ] Gradient definitions included if needed
- [ ] Optional: SVG optimization (remove unnecessary whitespace)
- [ ] Export tested with unit tests
- [ ] Generated SVG validates with W3C validator
- [ ] File size reasonable (< 50KB for typical animation)

#### Technical Notes
Enhanced implementation:
```typescript
class Animation {
  exportSVG(options?: { viewBox?: string, includeGradients?: boolean }): string {
    const { viewBox = '0 0 600 200', includeGradients = true } = options || {};

    const svg = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'svg');
    svg.setAttribute('xmlns', 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg');
    svg.setAttribute('viewBox', viewBox);

    if (includeGradients) {
      const defs = this.createGradientDefs();
      svg.appendChild(defs);
    }

    this.elements.forEach(element => {
      const elementSVG = element.toSVG();
      svg.appendChild(elementSVG);
    });

    return `<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>\n${svg.outerHTML}`;
  }
}
```

Test: `gallery/src/core/__tests__/SVGExport.test.ts`

